  <article class="asw-article">

  <div class="asw-answer" id="quick-answer">
    <p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> the average shoulder width is about <strong>16.4&nbsp;inches (41.6&nbsp;cm) for men</strong> and <strong>14.4&nbsp;inches (36.5&nbsp;cm) for women</strong>, measured bone to bone across the back. Measured across the deltoid muscles, the averages are about <strong>20.1&nbsp;in (51&nbsp;cm)</strong> for men and <strong>17.7&nbsp;in (45&nbsp;cm)</strong> for women.</p>
  </div>

